Flow mapping spread to K&R
description: the flow_map_spread state
- >
  THE SPREAD IS A PROPERTY OF THE WHOLE TOKEN, never of a level inside it: a nested `{a: [1]}` is
  ONE token (json5p expands everything under the switch), so Enter anywhere in it spreads from the
  OUTERMOST bracket and Backspace past any closer joins all of it. NO TRAPS AT THE EDGES - ENTER
  NEVER CLOSES a token (the closer does): on an empty cell it allocates the row and the caret
  STAYS inside, because a legal construct like `[12]` must never be a place where editing stops.
  An untyped element is dropped rather than written as `""`. PAST THE CLOSER Backspace STEPS BACK
  INSIDE, onto the token's last inner cell - it does NOT join (at document scale that reflowed a
  whole file under someone who was deleting, and asking for a container entry's own cell focused
  nothing at all, which was a lock). THE JOIN is the text editor's gesture instead: Backspace at
  the HEAD OF THE TOKEN'S FIRST LINE - every level from the outermost bracket down being element 0
  - pulls that line up onto the opener's and collapses the whole token. Just past the closer
  Backspace always has somewhere to go - it re-opens a cell inside an EMPTY token, joins a spread
  one, or steps onto the last cell. THE NEWLINE GESTURE. A comma keeps the next pair on this line;
  ENTER puts it on the next one, which SPREADS the token - one pair per row, the closer alone on
  the last. On disk that is an inline concrete switch to json5p (the
  [concretes](*::language:concretes) Collection style),
  so it is written by json5p's own serializer. The cells and the comma/closer grammar are
  unchanged; only the layout differs. A container json5p cannot hold - a keyed+keyless MIXTURE -
  does not spread, and the pair simply opens inline. Backspace just past the closer JOINS the
  token back onto one line (the caret stays in the after-cell)
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`key_colon_space`', '', '[value_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:value_hole)']
  - ['`close_brace`', '', '[scalar_committed](*::server:yamlover-editor:scalar_committed)']
  - ['`comma`', '', '`flow_map_spread` (stays)']
  - ['`enter`', 'otherwise', '`flow_map_spread` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the inner cell is empty and it is the only one', '[empty_cell_of_origin](*::server:yamlover-editor:empty_cell_of_origin)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the caret is past the closer', '[flow_map_editing](*::server:yamlover-editor:flow_map_editing)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'otherwise', '`flow_map_spread` (stays)']
